# 0009 — Linting rules

## 1. Description

New registry rules that bind conventions a skill can only describe: a file's
export surface, a file's role-named export, a role file's spec companion, a
barrel's export order, the ban on default exports, the ban on SCSS in `common/`,
provenance for breakpoints, colours, z-index and font size, the `it('should
<verb> …')` test-name form, the placement of a spec helper in its role file, and
the brace-free single-statement arrow body, the export shape of a feature's
queries object, validation bounds and patterns drawn from a constant, and
validation messages drawn from `ValidationMessage`, the resolver bound in its
schema file, one import per path and kind, the ban on `for` / `while` loops, and
a `TODO` that carries a ticket reference. Each is registered in
`rules/registry.ts` with scope, severity and a matching spec, following the shape
of the rules already shipping.

The candidates came from an audit of every `SKILL.md` and every example file
beside one — §5 holds the result. These twenty are the first pass; the remaining
`New` rows stay there until a later ticket picks them up.

